# Botium Toys - Controls & Compliance Checklist

This checklist summarizes the status of security controls and compliance best practices for Botium Toys based on the internal audit.

---

## Controls Assessment

| Control | In Place? | Notes |
|---------|-----------|-------|
| Least Privilege | No | All employees can access sensitive data; no restrictions in place. |
| Disaster Recovery Plans | No | No documented disaster recovery plan exists. |
| Password Policies | No | Weak password policy; not enforced with minimum complexity. |
| Separation of Duties | No | Not implemented; no role-based access controls. |
| Firewall | Yes | Firewall configured with appropriate security rules. |
| Intrusion Detection System (IDS) | No | IDS not installed or monitored. |
| Backups | No | No backups of critical data exist. |
| Antivirus Software | Yes | Installed and regularly monitored by IT. |
| Manual Monitoring/Maintenance for Legacy Systems | No | Legacy systems monitored inconsistently; no scheduled process. |
| Encryption | No | Customer credit card and PII data not encrypted. |
| Password Management System | No | No centralized password management system. |
| Locks (Offices, Storefront, Warehouse) | Yes | Physical locks are in place and functional. |
| CCTV Surveillance | Yes | CCTV is operational and monitored. |
| Fire Detection/Prevention | Yes | Fire alarms and sprinkler systems functional. |

---

## Compliance Assessment

### Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS)

| Best Practice | In Place? | Notes |
|---------------|-----------|-------|
| Only authorized users have access to customers’ credit card information | No | All employees have access. |
| Credit card information stored, accepted, processed, transmitted securely | No | No encryption in storage or transit. |
| Implement data encryption for credit card data | No | Encryption not implemented. |
| Adopt secure password management policies | No | Weak passwords, no centralized management. |

### General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)

| Best Practice | In Place? | Notes |
|---------------|-----------|-------|
| E.U. customers’ data is kept private/secured | No | Policies exist, but access control/encryption incomplete. |
| Breach notification within 72 hours | Yes | IT department has a plan in place. |
| Ensure data is properly classified and inventoried | No | Asset inventory and classification incomplete. |
| Enforce privacy policies, procedures, and processes | Yes | Policies and processes enforced internally. |

### System and Organization Controls (SOC Type 1 / SOC Type 2)

| Best Practice | In Place? | Notes |
|---------------|-----------|-------|
| User access policies are established | No | Password policy exists but weak; no access restrictions. |
| Sensitive data (PII/SPII) is confidential/private | No | All employees can access sensitive data; no encryption. |
| Data integrity ensures data is consistent, complete, accurate, validated | Yes | IT ensures integrated controls to maintain integrity. |
| Data is available to authorized individuals | Yes | Internal systems provide access as needed. |

---

## Recommendations (Optional)

- Implement **least privilege** and **separation of duties**.  
- Enforce **strong password policies** with centralized password management.  
- Encrypt all **sensitive customer data** (credit card info, PII).  
- Install and monitor an **Intrusion Detection System (IDS)**.  
- Develop and regularly test a **disaster recovery plan** and **backups**.  
- Complete a **full asset inventory** and classify assets based on criticality.  
- Address **PCI DSS, GDPR, and SOC compliance gaps**.
